a-end="927"><strong data-start="906" data-end="917">Protein</strong>: 10-15%</li><li data-start="928" data-end="945"><strong data-start="930" data-end="937">Fat</strong>: 2-4%</li><li data-start="946" data-end="968"><strong data-start="948" data-end="960">Moisture</strong>: ≤10%</li></ul><h2 data-start="970" data-end="997"><strong data-start="975" data-end="995">Key Applications</strong></h2><ol data-start="998" data-end="1759"><li data-start="998" data-end="1296"><p data-start="1001" data-end="1020"><strong data-start="1001" data-end="1018">Food Industry</strong></p><ul data-start="1024" data-end="1296"><li data-start="1024" data-end="1117"><strong data-start="1026" data-end="1046">Functional Foods</strong>: Used in granola bars, cereals, and protein powders for added fiber.</li><li data-start="1121" data-end="1215"><strong data-start="1123" data-end="1142">Baking Products</strong>: Enhances texture and nutritional value in bread, cakes, and pastries.</li><li data-start="1219" data-end="1296"><strong data-start="1221" data-end="1245">Beverage Supplements</strong>: Added to plant-based shakes and protein drinks.</li></ul></li><li data-start="1298" data-end="1496"><p data-start="1301" data-end="1318"><strong data-start="1301" data-end="1316">Animal Feed</strong></p><ul data-start="1322" data-end="1496"><li data-start="1322" data-end="1409"><strong data-start="1324" data-end="1357">Ruminant Feed (Cattle, Sheep)</strong>: Provides fermentable fiber to improve digestion.</li><li data-start="1413" data-end="1496"><strong data-start="1415" data-end="1427">Pet Food</strong>: Incorporated into dog and cat food for digestive health benefits.</li></ul></li><li data-start="1498" data-end="1759"><p data-start="1501" data-end="1539"><strong data-start="1501" data-end="1537">Functional Ingredient Extraction</strong></p><ul data-start="1543" data-end="1759"><li data-start="1543" data-end="1663"><strong data-start="1545" data-end="1566">Lignan Extraction</strong>: Used in antioxidant supplements for its anti-inflammatory and estrogen-regulating properties.</li><li data-start="1667" data-end="1759"><strong data-start="1669" data-end="1698">Dietary Fiber Supplements</strong>: Utilized as a fiber booster in various food formulations.</li></ul></li></ol><h2 data-start="1761" data-end="1786"><strong data-start="1766" data-end="1784">Specifications</strong></h2><ul data-start="1787" data-end="2060"><li data-start="1787" data-end="1851"><strong data-start="1789" data-end="1803">Appearance</strong>: Light brown to yellowish-brown powder/flakes</li><li data-start="1852" data-end="1901"><strong data-start="1854" data-end="1871">Particle Size</strong>: Customizable (20-100 mesh)</li><li data-start="1902" data-end="1932"><strong data-start="1904" data-end="1924">Moisture Content</strong>: ≤10%</li><li data-start="1933" data-end="1976"><strong data-start="1935" data-end="1953">Lignan Content</strong>: 1-4% (customizable)</li><li data-start="1977" data-end="2060"><strong data-start="1979" data-end="1992">Packaging</strong>: 25kg bags or bulk packaging, with customizable options available</li></ul><h2 data-start="2062" data-end="2093"><strong data-start="2067" data-end="2091">Storage &amp; Shelf Life</strong></h2><ul data-start="2094" data-end="2271"><li data-start="2094" data-end="2196"><strong data-start="2096" data-end="2118">Storage Conditions</strong>: Keep in a cool, dry, and well-ventilated place, away from direct sunlight.</li><li data-start="2197" data-end="2271"><strong data-start="2199" data-end="2213">Shelf Life</strong>: 24 months (unopened, under proper storage conditions).</li></ul><h2 data-start="2273" data-end="2298"><strong data-start="2278" data-end="2296">Key Advantages</strong></h2><ul data-start="2299" data-end="2635"><li data-start="2299" data-end="2370"><strong data-start="2301" data-end="2317">100% Natural</strong> – Free from artificial additives and preservatives</li><li data-start="2371" data-end="2468"><strong data-start="2373" data-end="2400">High in Lignans &amp; Fiber</strong> – Supports the development of functional and health food products</li><li data-start="2469" data-end="2540"><strong data-start="2471" data-end="2502">Customizable Particle Sizes</strong> – Suitable for various applications</li></ul><h2>FAQs about Flaxseed hull</h2><h3 data-start="76" data-end="113">1. <strong data-start="83" data-end="111">What are flaxseed hulls?</strong></h3><p data-start="114" data-end="328">Flaxseed hulls are the outer fiber-rich layer of flaxseeds, obtained as a byproduct after dehulling. They are rich in dietary fiber and lignans and are commonly used in food, animal feed, and dietary supplements.</p><h3 data-start="330" data-end="390">2. <strong data-start="337" data-end="388">What are the health benefits of flaxseed hulls?</strong></h3><p data-start="391" data-end="655">Flaxseed hulls are high in <strong data-start="418" data-end="429">lignans</strong>, which have antioxidant and estrogen-regulating properties that support cardiovascular health, reduce inflammation, and promote gut health. Additionally, their high dietary fiber content aids digestion and enhances satiety.</p><h3 data-start="657" data-end="722">3. <strong data-start="664" data-end="720">How are flaxseed hulls used in food and animal feed?</strong></h3><ul data-start="723" data-end="1013"><li data-start="723" data-end="877">In food, flaxseed hulls can be added to baked goods (such as bread and cookies) to increase dietary fiber content or used as a health food ingredient.</li><li data-start="878" data-end="1013">In animal feed, they serve as a high-quality fiber source that supports gut health, especially for ruminants, horses, and pet food.</li></ul><h3 data-start="1015" data-end="1059">4. <strong data-start="1022" data-end="1057">Are flaxseed hulls gluten-free?</strong></h3><p data-start="1060" data-end="1212">Yes. Flaxseed hulls are naturally <strong data-start="1094" data-end="1109">gluten-free</strong>, making them suitable for individuals with gluten sensitivities and those following a low-carb diet.</p><h3 data-start="1214" data-end="1291">5. <strong data-start="1221" data-end="1289">What is the difference between flaxseed hulls and flaxseed meal?</strong></h3><p data-start="1292" data-end="1492">Flaxseed hulls are the fibrous outer layer of flaxseeds, rich in lignans and insoluble dietary fiber, whereas <strong data-start="1402" data-end="1419">flaxseed meal</strong> is made from ground whole flaxseeds and contains more protein and oil.</p><h3 data-start="1494" data-end="1565">6. <strong data-start="1501" data-end="1563">How should flaxseed hulls be stored to maintain freshness?</strong></h3><p data-start="1566" data-end="1761">It is recommended to store flaxseed hulls in a <strong data-start="1613" data-end="1632">cool, dry place</strong>, away from direct sunlight. For long-term storage, keep them sealed and refrigerated to prevent oxidation and moisture damage.</p></div><div class="woocommerce-Tabs-panel woocommerce-Tabs-panel--reviews panel entry-content wc-tab" id="tab-reviews" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-title-reviews"><div id="reviews" class="woocommerce-Reviews"><div id="comments"><h2 class="woocommerce-Reviews-title">
